{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788305418,"nonce":"WoYmcyJcSJpAjhwX3AFgObByeDo=","message":"THE CONCRETE BLOCKER, MEASURED, and the reason prison is OUT OF SCOPE for the M1 re-run. Session 21, orchestrator.\n\nEvan asked whether the M1 re-run could include a prison. It cannot, and this is exactly why — one missing write.\n\n## The finding\n\n`grep -rn \"ForPrisoners\" Source/AutoRimmer/` returns **three reads and no writes**:\n\n- `PawnEmergencyVerbs.cs` — a gate (`bed.ForPrisoners || !bed.Medical` -\u003e `not-medical`)\n- `PlaceVerbs.cs` — published as `for_prisoners` on a bed's row\n- `TemperatureVerbs.cs` — named in a comment about `Building_Bed.ForPrisoners` being scribed\n\n**`Building_Bed.ForPrisoners` is never SET.** The observation surface reports whether a bed is a prisoner bed and no verb can make one.\n\n`warden` is not the missing piece and it is worth being precise about why: its ops are `mode` (`enable`/`disable`), `recruitable` and `clear` — the prisoner INTERACTION mode, i.e. what a warden does to a prisoner who already exists in a cell. It presupposes the prison.\n\n## So the chain breaks in the middle\n\n`arrest` ships. `capture` ships. `warden` ships. What does not ship is the one step between them: **designating the bed that makes a room a prison.** Without it a captured pawn has nowhere to be a prisoner, so `warden`'s modes have no subject and recruitment — the main population-growth path, and therefore the main THRIVE lever — is unreachable.\n\nThe verb is small. `ForPrisoners` is a settable property on `Building_Bed`, and the shape is `warden`'s: address a bed, set a flag, journal it, report per-bed refusals. The gate to re-implement is the widget one — RimWorld puts prisoner-bed designation in the bed's own gizmo/inspect pane, so per DESIGN §Action model that member is what a player verb must cite.\n\nNote the hazard flagged on `d16a463` while you are here: `Building_Bed.ForPrisoners` is reached by `RegionGrid.GetValidRegionAt`'s room rebuild path, which is scribed. An observer that touches it can mutate; a SETTER is allowed to, but should not do so as a side effect of a read.\n\n## Why it is not being done now\n\nEvan, session 21: *\"no prison is fine ... we'll make sure prisoners is filed but that's another day's work.\"* The M1 re-run is scoped to a base, a farm and a militia; workshop and rec room are both reachable today (`build` is def-driven and `room` publishes `role`, so a rec room is verifiable rather than claimable), and prison is the one of the three that is not.\n\nThis comment is the filing he asked for.\n\n## Suggested Acceptance, for when it is picked up\n\n- A verb sets `ForPrisoners` on a named bed and clears it, journalled both ways, and `things`/`place` reports `for_prisoners` flipping to match.\n- The widget precondition is re-implemented and cited by file + member.\n- A bed that cannot be a prisoner bed is refused BY NAME with the game's own reason, not skipped.\n- A room containing only prisoner beds reports the prison role the game gives it, so \"is this a prison\" is a read rather than an inference.\n- End to end on a bench: `arrest` -\u003e `capture` -\u003e a designated prisoner bed -\u003e `warden {recruitable}` -\u003e the prisoner is recruitable. Each step journalled. That chain is the actual deliverable; the flag alone is not.","files":null}]}